  <h1>Open-source cloud security docs</h1>
  <p>
    OpenSourceOM Core is a self-hosted security graph. Collectors pull cloud and Kubernetes inventory
    into PostgreSQL. Named path queries, CSPM rules, and CVE enrichment rank what an outsider can
    reach. These pages describe the <code>om</code> CLI, REST API, and collectors as they ship in
    <a href="https://github.com/OpenSourceOM/core">OpenSourceOM/core</a> (Phase 3).
  </p>

  <h2>Start</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/docs/getting-started/">Getting started</a> — Compose, migrations, the demo graph, and a first scan</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/configuration/">Configuration</a> — environment variables for the CLI and API</li>
  </ul>

